Fan.description:
DIV{HEADER1{Fan,  -- the class of all fans}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, A Fan represents a fan of rational convex polyhedral cones, i.e. a collection of cones, such that for every cone in the fan all faces are in the fan and for every two cones in the fan their intersection is a face of each (intersection condition). It need not be full dimensional or pure, and the cones need not be pointed. It is saved as a hash table which contains a list of the generating cones of the fan starting with those of maximal dimension. So for every cone in this list all faces are considered to be in the fan. The output of a Fan looks like this:, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : normalFan crossPolytope 3

o1 = Fan{...1...}

o1 : Fan, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{}, This table displays a short summary of the properties of the Fan. However, one can not access the above information directly, because this is just a virtual hash table generated for the output. The data defining a Fan is extracted by the functions included in this package. A Fan can be constructed by collecting Cones that satisfy the intersection condition. Every cone that is added to a Fan is always considered as the collection of the Cone and all of its faces., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{2,2},{1,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{2,-2},{1,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : C3 = coneFromVData matrix {{-2,-2},{1,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : C4 = coneFromVData matrix {{-2,2},{-1,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : F = fan {C1,C2,C3,C4}

o6 = F

o6 : Fan, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{}, This fan is for example the normal fan of a ''flattened'' crosspolytope in 2-space., PARA{},  See also , TO{Polyhedra :: Working with fans}, .}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Functions and methods returning , an object of class Fan, :}, UL{LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: ccRefinement}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: faceFan}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: fan}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: hirzebruch}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: imageFan}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: normalFan}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: skeleton}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: smoothSubfan}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{stellarSubdivision(Fan,Matrix)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: stellarSubdivision}}}}, HEADER2{Methods that use , an object of class Fan, :}, UL{LI{SPAN{KBD{addCone(Cone,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: addCone}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{addCone(List,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: addCone}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: addCone(Fan,Cone)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{commonFace(Cone,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: commonFace}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{commonFace(Fan,Cone)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: commonFace}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{commonFace(Fan,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: commonFace}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{cones(ZZ,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: cones}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{contains(Fan,Cone)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: contains}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: directProduct(Fan,Fan)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{facesAsCones(ZZ,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: facesAsCones}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: Fan * Fan}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: Fan == Fan}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompCones(Cone,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompCones}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompCones(Fan,Cone)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompCones}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompCones(Fan,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompCones}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isComplete(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isComplete}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isPointed(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isPointed}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isPolytopal(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isPolytopal}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isPure(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isPure}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isSmooth(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isSmooth(Cone)}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isWellDefined(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isWellDefined(Cone)}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: linearTransform(Fan,Matrix)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{linSpace(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: linSpace}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{maxCones(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: maxCones}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: minimalNonFaces(Fan)}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex(Fan)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{polytope(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: polytope}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{skeleton(ZZ,Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: skeleton}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{smoothSubfan(Fan)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: smoothSubfan}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: stanleyReisnerRing(Fan)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Type, type}}, , with ancestor classes , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralObject},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: MutableHashTable},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: Thing}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:310:0}, .}}}}

fan.description:
DIV{HEADER1{fan,  -- generates a Fan}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{F = fan C , class => language-macaulay2}}, DD{CODE{F = fan L, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{C}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Polyhedra :: Cone, convex rational cone}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{L}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: List, list}}, , , with elements of class , TO{Polyhedra :: Cone},  or , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{F}, , , SPAN{an instance of the type , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan}}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{},  If , TT{fan},  is applied to a , TO{Polyhedra :: Cone},  it generates the , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan},  given by the Cone and all of its faces. If applied to a , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: List},  the list must only contain Cones and Fans in the same ambient space. Then it adds the Cones in the List and the generating Cones of the Fans in the List one by one to the Fan, checking each time if the new Cone is compatible with the cones that have already been added, i.e. that the intersection with each of them is a face of both Cones (intersection condition)., PARA{}, If one of the cones is in the wrong ambient space, there will be an error and no fan will be returned. If the intersection condition fails, there will also be an error. The pairs of incompatible cones can be accessed with the function , TO{Polyhedra :: incompCones}, ., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,-1},{0,-1}}

o1 = C

o1 : Cone, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : F = fan C

o2 = F

o2 : Fan, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,0},{0,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{0,-1},{1,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : F = fan {C,C1,C2}

o5 = F

o5 : Fan, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{fan}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{fan(Cone)}}, LI{KBD{fan(List)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{fan(Matrix,List)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(Matrix,Matrix,List)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{fan(Matrix,Matrix,Sequence)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{fan(Matrix,Sequence)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(PolyhedralComplex)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: fan},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:594:0}, .}}}}

