hilbertBasis.description:
DIV{HEADER1{hilbertBasis,  -- computes the Hilbert basis of a Cone}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{HB = hilbertBasis C, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{C}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Polyhedra :: Cone, convex rational cone}}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{L}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: List, list}}, , , containing the elements of the Hilbert basis}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{}, The Hilbert basis of the cone , TT{C},  is computed by the Project-and-Lift-algorithm by Raymond Hemmecke (see below). It computes a Hilbert basis of the cone modulo the lineality space, so it returns the list of one column matrices that give the Hilbert basis of the Cone if one adds the basis of the lineality space and its negative. For the Project-and-Lift-algorithm see: , PARA{}, HREF{http://www.hemmecke.de/raymond/, Raymond Hemmecke's},  , EM{On the computation of Hilbert bases of cones}, , in A. M. Cohen, X.-S. Gao, and N. Takayama, editors, Mathematical Software, ICMS 2002, pages 307317. World Scientific, 2002., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}}

o1 = C

o1 : Cone, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : hilbertBasis C

o2 = {| 1 |, | 1 |, | 2 |}
      | 1 |  | 2 |  | 1 |

o2 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{}, Beginning with Macaulay2 version 1.24.11, this method calls the internal function , TT{rawHilbertBasis},  which calls the C++ library , TO2{Polyhedra :: normaliz, libnormaliz}, .}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{FourTiTwo :: hilbertBasis(Matrix)}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{hilbertBasis}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{hilbertBasis(Cone)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: hilbertBasis},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunctionWithOptions, method function with options}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:1626:0}, .}}}}

