incompCones.description:
DIV{HEADER1{incompCones,  -- returns the pairs of incompatible cones}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{Lpairs = incompCones L , class => language-macaulay2}}, DD{CODE{Lpairs = incompCones(X,F) , class => language-macaulay2}}, DD{CODE{Lpairs = incompCones(F,X), class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{L}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: List, list}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{F}, , , SPAN{an instance of the type , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{X}, , , TO{Polyhedra :: Cone},  or , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{Lpairs}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: List, list}}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{}, If , TT{incompCones},  is applied to a list of cones and fans, then it returns the pairs of elements whose intersection is not a face of each. For a cone , TT{C},  and a fan , TT{F},  in the list this means there is at least one generating cone of , TT{F},  whose intersection with , TT{C},  is not a face of each. For two fans in the list this means there is at least one generating cone each such that their intersection is not a face of each. If applied to a pair consisting of a cone and a fan or two fans, then it returns the pairs of cones that do not share a common face., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix{{1,0},{1,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix{{1,0},{0,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : C3 = coneFromVData matrix{{-1,0},{0,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : C4 = coneFromVData matrix{{1,1},{0,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : C5 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : L = {C1,C2,C3,C4,C5};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i7 : Lpairs = incompCones L

o7 = {(C1, C5), (C4, C5)}

o7 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i8 : Lpairs == {(C1,C4),(C1,C5)}

o8 = false, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{incompCones}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{incompCones(Cone,Fan)}}, LI{KBD{incompCones(Fan,Cone)}}, LI{KBD{incompCones(Fan,Fan)}}, LI{KBD{incompCones(List)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: incompCones},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:1659:0}, .}}}}

