Isomorphism.description:
DIV{HEADER1{Isomorphism,  -- probabilistic test for isomorphism of modules}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, DIV{PARA{TEX{Two modules are isomorphic if there a homomorphism $f:M \to N$ which is both injective and surjective, or equivalently if there is a surjection in each direction. These routines produce random combinations of the generators of }, TO{Macaulay2Doc :: Hom}, TEX{ and test for a homomorphism which is both injective and surjective.}}, PARA{TEX{Note that it suffices to check surjectivity after tensoring with the residue field, so in a future version we may instead check for surjections in both directions.}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Contributors}, DIV{PARA{TEX{Mike Stillman and Devlin Mallory contributed to this package.}}, PARA{}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: isIsomorphic}}, LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: isomorphism}}, LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: checkDegrees}}}}, DIV{DIV{DIV{HEADER2{Authors}, UL{LI{HREF{https://eisenbud.github.io, David Eisenbud}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:de@berkeley.edu, de@berkeley.edu}, >}}, LI{HREF{https://mahrud.github.io, Mahrud Sayrafi}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:mahrud@umn.edu, mahrud@umn.edu}, >}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Version}, PARA{This documentation describes version , BOLD{2.0},  of , Isomorphism, , released , BOLD{April 30, 2025}, .}}, DIV{HEADER2{Citation}, PARA{If you have used , this package,  in your research, please cite it as follows:}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{class => language-bib, @misc{IsomorphismSource,
  title = {{Isomorphism: probabilistic test of isomorphism between modules. Version~2.0}},
  author = {David Eisenbud and Mahrud Sayrafi},
  howpublished = {A \emph{Macaulay2} package available at
    \url{https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/tree/stable/M2/Macaulay2/packages}}
}
}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Exports}, DIV{class => exports, UL{LI{Functions and commands, UL{LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: checkDegrees}}, LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: isIsomorphic}}, LI{TOH{Isomorphism :: isomorphism}}}}, LI{Methods, UL{LI{SPAN{KBD{checkDegrees(Matrix,Matrix)},  -- see , TOH{Isomorphism :: checkDegrees}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{checkDegrees(Module,Module)},  -- see , TOH{Isomorphism :: checkDegrees}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isIsomorphic(Matrix,Matrix)},  -- see , TOH{Isomorphism :: isIsomorphic}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isIsomorphic(Module,Module)},  -- see , TOH{Isomorphism :: isIsomorphic}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isomorphism(Module,Module)},  -- see , TOH{Isomorphism :: isomorphism}}}}}}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Isomorphism :: Isomorphism},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Package, package}}, , defined in , TT{Isomorphism.m2}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Isomorphism.m2:528:0}, .}}}}

isPolytopal.description:
DIV{HEADER1{isPolytopal,  -- checks if a Fan is polytopal}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{b = isPolytopal F, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{F}, , , SPAN{an instance of the type , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan}}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{b}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Boolean, Boolean value}}, , , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: true},  if the , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan},  is polytopal, , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: false},  otherwise}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{}, If , TT{F},  is projective, then there exists a polyhedron , TT{P},  such that , TT{F},  is the normalFan of , TT{P}, . This means every codimension 1 cone of the Fan corresponds exactly to an edge of the polytope. So consider , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: QQ},  to the number of all edges. This can be considered as the space of all edge lengths. If we take arbitrary lengths now for every edge we do not get a polytope. But every codimension 2 cone of the fan corresponds to a 2 dimensional face of the polytope and if the edges belonging to this face add up to 0 zero, they form in fact a 2 dimensional face. This gives linear equations on the space of edge lengths and if we intersect these equations with the positive orthant in the space of edge lengths we get a Cone. Thus, there exists such a polytope if and only if there is a vector in this cone with strictly positive entries, since every edge has to appear in the polytope., PARA{}, IF , TT{F},  is polytopal, the function , TO{Polyhedra :: polytope},  returns a polytope of which , TT{F},  is the normalFan., PARA{}, Note that the function first checks if the fan is complete., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,0},{0,1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,-1},{0,-2}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : C3 = coneFromVData matrix {{0,-2},{1,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : C4 = coneFromVData matrix {{-1,-2},{-2,-1}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : F = fan{C1,C2,C3,C4}

o5 = F

o5 : Fan, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : isPolytopal F

o6 = true, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{isPolytopal}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{isPolytopal(Fan)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: isPolytopal},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:1380:0}, .}}}}

