newClass.description:
DIV{HEADER1{newClass,  -- set the class and parent of an object}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, DIV{HEADER2{setting the class and parent}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{newClass(A,B,x), class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{A}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable, hash table}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{B}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable, hash table}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{x}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{a copy (possibly) of , TT{x},  with , TT{A},  as class and , TT{B},  as parent}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{setting the class}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{newClass(A,x), class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{A}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable, hash table}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{x}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{a copy (possibly) of , TT{x},  with , TT{A},  as the new class}}}}}}, HEADER2{common remarks}, PARA{If , TT{x},  is a basic list or sequence, then , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: BasicList},  should be an ancestor of , TT{A},  and , TT{B},  should be , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: Nothing}, . If , TT{x},  is a hash table, then , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable},  should be an ancestor of , TT{A}, .}, PARA{If the class (and parent) of x are already equal to A (and B, respectively), then copying of the elements of , TT{x},  is not required, and is not done.}, PARA{If , TT{x},  is mutable, and instances of class , TT{A},  are also mutable, then copying of the elements of , TT{x},  is not required, and is not done.}, PARA{If , TT{x},  is not a hash table, basic list, or sequence, then its class will be set to , TT{A},  internally, essentially by wrapping it in a special kind of object designed solely to indicate the new class.  The new class , TT{A},  must be a specialization of the class of , TT{x}, . The parent cannot be reset this way. Not all of the internal code of Macaulay2 is ready to recognize such wrapped objects, which are part of a new feature, except for the code that handles functions.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : t = 1..4

o1 = (1, 2, 3, 4)

o1 : Sequence, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : newClass(Array,t)

o2 = [1, 2, 3, 4]

o2 : Array, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : x = new HashTable from { a => 1, b => 2 }

o3 = HashTable{a => 1}
               b => 2

o3 : HashTable, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : z = newClass(ImmutableType,Vector,x)

o4 = ImmutableType{a => 1}
                   b => 2

o4 : ImmutableType, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : parent z

o5 = Vector

o5 : Type, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{The difference between , TT{new A of B from x},  and , TT{newClass(A,B,x)},  is that the methods installed for , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: new},  are not used.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : new Thing of Thing from Thing := (A,B,c) -> ( 
            << "-- new " << A << " of " << B
            << " from " << toString c << endl;
            c);, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i7 : new ImmutableType of Vector from x
-- new ImmutableType of Vector from new HashTable from {a => 1, b => 2}

o7 = ImmutableType{a => 1}
                   b => 2

o7 : ImmutableType, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i8 : newClass(ImmutableType,Vector,x)

o8 = ImmutableType{a => 1}
                   b => 2

o8 : ImmutableType, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: new}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: copy}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: toList}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: newClass},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: CompiledFunction, compiled function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Macaulay2Doc/ov_types.m2:435:0}, .}}}}

