Parsing.description:
DIV{HEADER1{Parsing,  -- a framework for building parsers}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{TO{Parsing :: Parsing},  is a package the provides a framework for building parsers.  It introduces , TO{Parsing :: Parser}, , a type of function that parses a sequence of tokens, and , TO{Parsing :: Analyzer}, , a type of function that accepts input for the parser in its original form and separates it into a stream of tokens.  A parser can be combined with an analyzer: see , TO{Parsing :: Parser : Analyzer}, , to produce a complete system for accepting input and parsing it.}, PARA{See the package , TO{Classic :: Classic},  for a good example of  the use of this framework.}}, MENU{TO{Parsing :: Analyzer}, TO{Parsing :: Parser}, TO{Parsing :: Parser : Analyzer}}, DIV{DIV{DIV{HEADER2{Author}, UL{LI{HREF{http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~dan/, Daniel R. Grayson}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:dan@math.uiuc.edu, dan@math.uiuc.edu}, >}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Version}, PARA{This documentation describes version , BOLD{1.0},  of , Parsing, , released , BOLD{June, 2006}, .}}, DIV{HEADER2{Citation}, PARA{If you have used , this package,  in your research, please cite it as follows:}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{class => language-bib, @misc{ParsingSource,
  title = {{Parsing: a framework for creating recursive descent parsers. Version~1.0}},
  author = {Daniel R. Grayson},
  howpublished = {A \emph{Macaulay2} package available at
    \url{https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/tree/stable/M2/Macaulay2/packages}}
}
}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Exports}, DIV{class => exports, UL{LI{Types, UL{LI{TOH{Parsing :: Analyzer}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: Parser}}}}, LI{Functions and commands, UL{LI{TOH{Parsing :: andP}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: charAnalyzer}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: constParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: deadParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: futureParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: letterParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: NNParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: nonspaceAnalyzer}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: nullParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: optionalSignParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: optP}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: orP}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: QQParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: terminalParser}}, LI{TOH{Parsing :: ZZParser}}}}, LI{Symbols, UL{LI{TOH{Parsing :: nil}}}}}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Parsing :: Parsing},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Package, package}}, , defined in , TT{Parsing.m2}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Parsing.m2:184:0}, .}}}}

