Polyhedra.description:
DIV{HEADER1{Polyhedra,  -- for computations with convex polyhedra, cones, and fans}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, A rational convex , TO{Polyhedra :: Polyhedron},  is the intersection of finitely many affine half-spaces over , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: QQ},  or equivalently, the convex hull of a finite set of vertices and rays. A rational convex polyhedral , TO{Polyhedra :: Cone},  is the intersection of finitely many linear half-spaces over , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: QQ},  or equivalently, the positive hull of a finite set of rays. A , TO{Polyhedra :: Fan},  is a finite collection of cones such that for each cone all its faces are in the fan and for two cones in the fan the intersection is a face of each., PARA{}, TT{Polyhedra},  uses the , UL{LI{TO{FourierMotzkin :: FourierMotzkin},  package by , HREF{http://www.mast.queensu.ca/~ggsmith, Gregory G. Smith}}, LI{TO{FourTiTwo :: FourTiTwo},  package by , HREF{http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~mike/, Michael Stillman}, , , HREF{http://people.math.gatech.edu/~jyu67/, Josephine Yu}, , and , HREF{http://math.iit.edu/~spetrov1/, Sonja Petrovic}}, LI{TO{Normaliz :: Normaliz},  package by Gesa Kaempf and Christof Soeger}, LI{TO{Topcom :: Topcom},  package by , HREF{http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~mike/, Michael Stillman}, .}}, PARA{}, Here are some examples illustrating the main uses of this package., UL{LI{TO{Polyhedra :: Working with polyhedra}}, LI{TO{Polyhedra :: Working with cones}}, LI{TO{Polyhedra :: Working with fans}}}, PARA{}, Please have a look at , TO{Polyhedra :: V- and H-representation},  on conventions used throughout this package before you start., PARA{}, For an introduction to polyhedra and cones, we recommend , HREF{http://www.mi.fu-berlin.de/math/groups/discgeom/ziegler/, Gunter M. Ziegler's},  , EM{Lectures on Polytopes}, , Graduate Texts in Mathematics 152, Springer-Verlag, New York, 1995., PARA{}, The authors would like to thank , UL{LI{HREF{https://faculty.math.illinois.edu/~dan/, Daniel R. Grayson}}, LI{HREF{http://people.cs.uchicago.edu/~nilten/, Nathan Ilten}}, LI{HREF{http://page.math.tu-berlin.de/~panizzut/, Marta Panizzut}}, LI{HREF{http://www.mast.queensu.ca/~ggsmith/, Gregory G. Smith}}, LI{HREF{http://astaal.be/, Andrew P. Staal}}, LI{HREF{http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~mike/, Michael Stillman}}, LI{HREF{http://www.mi.fu-berlin.de/math/groups/ag-algebra/members/mitarbeiter/Winz.html, Anna-Lena Winz}}}, for code contributions, bug reports, and helpful discussions concerning this package.}, DIV{DIV{DIV{HEADER2{Authors}, UL{LI{HREF{http://page.mi.fu-berlin.de/rbirkner/index.htm, René Birkner}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:rbirkner@mi.fu-berlin.de, rbirkner@mi.fu-berlin.de}, >}}, LI{HREF{http://page.mi.fu-berlin.de/lkastner/, Lars Kastner}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:k.l@fu-berlin.de, k.l@fu-berlin.de}, >}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Certification , IMG{src => common/share/Macaulay2/Style/GoldStar.png, alt => a gold star}}, PARA{Version , BOLD{1.0.5},  of this package,  was accepted for publication,  in , HREF{https://msp.org/jsag/2009/1-1/, volume 1},  of , HREF{https://msp.org/jsag/, The Journal of Software for Algebra and Geometry: Macaulay2},  on , 2009-09-07, , in the article , HREF{https://msp.org/jsag/2009/1-1/p03.xhtml, Polyhedra: a package for computations with convex polyhedral objects},  (DOI: , HREF{https://doi.org/10.2140/jsag.2009.1.11, 10.2140/jsag.2009.1.11}, ). That version can be obtained,  from , HREF{https://msp.org/jsag/2009/1-1/jsag-v1-n1-x03-code.zip, the journal}, .}}, DIV{HEADER2{Version}, PARA{This documentation describes version , BOLD{1.10},  of , Polyhedra, , released , BOLD{November 12, 2018}, .}}, DIV{HEADER2{Citation}, PARA{If you have used , this package,  in your research, please cite it as follows:}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{class => language-bib, @misc{PolyhedraSource,
  title = {{Polyhedra: convex polyhedra. Version~1.10}},
  author = {Ren{\'e} Birkner and Lars Kastner},
  howpublished = {A \emph{Macaulay2} package available at
    \url{https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/tree/stable/M2/Macaulay2/packages}}
}

