PolyhedralComplex.description:
DIV{HEADER1{PolyhedralComplex,  -- the class of all polyhedral complexes}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, A PolyhedralComplex represents a complex of rational convex polyhedra, i.e. a collection of polyhedra, such that for every polyhedron in the complex all faces are in the complex and for every two polyhedra in the complex their intersection is a face of each (intersection condition). It need not be full dimensional or pure, and the polyhedra need not be compact. It is saved as a hash table which contains a list of the generating polyhedra of the complex starting with those of maximal dimension. So for every polyhedron in this list all faces are considered to be in the complex. The output of a PolyhedralComplex looks like this:, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : polyhedralComplex crossPolytope 3

o1 = PolyhedralComplex{...1...}

o1 : PolyhedralComplex, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{}, This table displays a short summary of the properties of the PolyhedralComplex. However, one can not access the above information directly, because this is just a virtual hash table generated for the output. The data defining a PolyhedralComplex is extracted by the functions included in this package. A PolyhedralComplex can be constructed by collecting Polyhedra that satisfy the intersection condition. Every polyhedron that is added to a PolyhedralComplex is always considered as the collection of the Polyhedron and all of its faces., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : P1 = convexHull matrix {{2,2,0},{1,-1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : P2 = convexHull matrix {{2,-2,0},{1,1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : P3 = convexHull matrix {{-2,-2,0},{1,-1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : P4 = convexHull matrix {{-2,2,0},{-1,-1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : F = polyhedralComplex {P1,P2,P3,P4}

o6 = F

o6 : PolyhedralComplex, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Methods that use , an object of class PolyhedralComplex, :}, UL{LI{SPAN{KBD{addPolyhedron(List,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: addPolyhedron}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{addPolyhedron(Polyhedron,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: addPolyhedron}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: fan(PolyhedralComplex)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompPolyhedra(PolyhedralComplex,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompPolyhedra}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompPolyhedra(PolyhedralComplex,Polyhedron)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompPolyhedra}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{incompPolyhedra(Polyhedron,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: incompPolyhedra}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isComplete(PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isComplete}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isPure(PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isPure}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{isWellDefined(PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: isWellDefined(Cone)}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{maxPolyhedra(PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: maxPolyhedra}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{polyhedra(ZZ,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedra}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{skeleton(ZZ,PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: skeleton}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{vertices(PolyhedralComplex)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: vertices}}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralComplex},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Type, type}}, , with ancestor classes , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralObject},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: MutableHashTable},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: HashTable},  < , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: Thing}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:343:0}, .}}}}

polyhedralComplex.description:
DIV{HEADER1{polyhedralComplex,  -- generates a PolyhedralComplex}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{PC = polyhedralComplex P , class => language-macaulay2}}, DD{CODE{PC = polyhedralComplex L, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{P}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Polyhedra :: Polyhedron, convex polyhedron}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{L}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: List, list}}, , , with elements of class , TO{Polyhedra :: Polyhedron},  or , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralComplex}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{F}, , , SPAN{an instance of the type , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralComplex}}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, PARA{},  If , TT{polyhedralComplex},  is applied to a , TO{Polyhedra :: Polyhedron},  it generates the , TO{Polyhedra :: PolyhedralComplex},  given by the Polyhedron and all of its faces. If applied to a , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: List},  the list must only contain Polyhedra and PolyhedralComplexes in the same ambient space. Then it adds the Polyhedra in the List and the generating Polyhedra of the PolyhedralComplexes in the List one by one to the new PolyhedralComplex, checking each time if the new Polyhedron is compatible with the polyhedra that have already been added, i.e. that the intersection with each of them is a face of both Polyhedra (intersection condition)., PARA{}, If one of the polyhedra is in the wrong ambient space (i.e. not the ambient space of the first object in the list), then there will be an error and no PolyhedralComplex will be returned. If the intersection condition fails, there will also be an error. The pairs of incompatible polyhedra can be accessed with the function , TO{Polyhedra :: incompPolyhedra}, ., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : P = convexHull matrix {{1,-1,0},{0,-1,0}}

o1 = P

o1 : Polyhedron, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : PC = polyhedralComplex P

o2 = PC

o2 : PolyhedralComplex, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : P1 = convexHull matrix {{1,0,0},{0,1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : P2 = convexHull matrix {{0,-1,0},{1,-1,0}};, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : PC = polyhedralComplex {PC,P1,P2}

o5 = PC

o5 : PolyhedralComplex, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{polyhedralComplex}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{polyhedralComplex(List)}}, LI{KBD{polyhedralComplex(Polyhedron)}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex(Fan)}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{polyhedralComplex(Matrix,List)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}, LI{SPAN{KBD{polyhedralComplex(Matrix,Matrix,List)},  -- see , TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}, LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex(Matrix,Matrix,Matrix,List)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Polyhedra :: polyhedralComplex},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Polyhedra/documentation/old_documentation.m2:630:0}, .}}}}

