same.description:
DIV{HEADER1{same,  -- whether everything in a list is the same}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{same L, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{L}, , , TEX{a list}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{b}, , , TEX{a Boolean}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : same {1, 1, 1, 1}

o1 = true, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : same {1, 2, 1, 1}

o2 = false, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, DIV{PARA{TEX{The comparison is done with "===", which is quick, but not always intuitive. Here is a simple example of what can go wrong:}}}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : R = QQ[x,y,z];, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : L = {gcd{x,y}, x/x, 1}

o4 = {1, 1, 1}

o4 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : same L

o5 = false, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, DIV{PARA{TEX{We can see the problem by asking , TT{Macaulay2},  to display the class of each element of , TT{L}, . (Or use the function }, TO{Macaulay2Doc :: uniform}, TEX{, which returns whether or not the elements of a list are all of the same class.)}}}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : apply(L, class)

o6 = {R, frac R, ZZ}

o6 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i7 : uniform L

o7 = false, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, DIV{PARA{TEX{The first , TT{1},  is an element of the ring , TT{R}, , the second , TT{1},  is an element of the fraction field of , TT{R}, , and the third , TT{1},  is an integer. Thus , TT{Macaulay2},  thinks of these three elements as being pairwise unequal, with respect to the operator "===".}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: commonest}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: number}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: set}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: uniform}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: unique}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: lists and sequences}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: same},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: FunctionClosure, function closure}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Macaulay2Doc/functions/same-doc.m2:48:0}, .}}}}

