o2 = /tmp/M2-710672-0/1.html, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{This function will work under Unix, and also under Windows if you have a directory on the same drive called , TT{/tmp}, .}, PARA{If the name of the temporary file will be given to an external program, it may be necessary to concatenate it with , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: rootPath},  or , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: rootURI},  to enable the external program to find the file.}, PARA{The temporary file name is derived from the value of the environment variable , TT{TMPDIR}, , if it has one.}, PARA{If , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: fork},  is used, then the parent and child Macaulay2 processes will each remove their own temporary files upon termination, with the parent removing any files created before , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: fork},  was called.}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: File}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: rootPath}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: rootURI}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: temporaryFileName},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: FunctionClosure, function closure}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Macaulay2Doc/ov_system.m2:1433:0}, .}}}}

terms.description:
DIV{HEADER1{terms,  -- provide a list of terms of a polynomial}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, DIV{HEADER2{Synopsis}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{terms f, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{f}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: RingElement, ring element}}, , , in a polynomial ring , TT{R},  with coefficient ring , TT{A}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{the list of terms of , TT{f}}}}}}, Each term is an element of the coefficient ring , TT{A}, , multiplied with a  monomial in the variables of , TT{R}, ., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : R = QQ[a..d];, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : terms(a+d^2-1+a*b*c)

              2
o2 = {a*b*c, d , a, -1}

o2 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, In the situation where the ring is a polynomial ring over another polynomial ring, the polynomial is split using the monomials of the outer ring., TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : S = R[x,y];, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i4 : terms(a*x+b*x+c*x*y+c*x^3+1+a)

         3
o4 = {c*x , c*x*y, (a + b)x, a + 1}

o4 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Synopsis}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{terms(k,f), class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{k}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Ring, ring}}}}, LI{SPAN{TT{f}, , , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: RingElement, ring element}}, , , in a polynomial ring , TT{R}}}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{the list of terms of , TT{f},  with , TT{k},  regarded as the coefficient ring}}}}}, PARA{Each term is an element of the coefficient ring , TT{k}, , multiplied with a monomial in the variables of , TT{R}, . This is useful in the situation where the polynomial , TT{R},  is built from , TT{k},  by a sequence of extensions.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : R = QQ[a][d];, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i6 : f = (1+a+d)^3

      3            2      2               3     2
o6 = d  + (3a + 3)d  + (3a  + 6a + 3)d + a  + 3a  + 3a + 1

o6 : R, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i7 : terms f

       3           2     2              3     2
o7 = {d , (3a + 3)d , (3a  + 6a + 3)d, a  + 3a  + 3a + 1}

o7 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i8 : terms(QQ,f)

       3      2    2    2              3    2
o8 = {d , 3a*d , 3d , 3a d, 6a*d, 3d, a , 3a , 3a, 1}

o8 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: coefficients}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: monomials}}, LI{TOH{Macaulay2Doc :: someTerms}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{terms}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{terms(Ring,RingElement)}}, LI{KBD{terms(RingElement)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: terms},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{Macaulay2Doc/functions/terms-doc.m2:51:0}, .}}}}

