DIV{HEADER1{topComponents,  -- compute top dimensional component of an ideal or module}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{topComponents M, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{Inputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{TT{M}, , , SPAN{an , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Ideal, ideal}},  or , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Module, module}}, , }}}}, LI{Outputs:, UL{LI{SPAN{SPAN{an , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Ideal, ideal}},  or , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: Module, module}}, , , TEX{the intersection of the primary components of the input with the greatest Krull dimension}}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, DIV{PARA{TEX{The method used is that of Eisenbud-Huneke-Vasconcelos, in their 1993 Inventiones Mathematicae paper.}}}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a..c];, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i2 : I = intersect(ideal(a,b), ideal(b,c), ideal(c,a), ideal(a^2,b^3,c^4));

o2 : Ideal of R, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : topComponents I

o3 = ideal (b*c, a*c, a*b)

o3 : Ideal of R, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, DIV{PARA{TEX{If $M$ is a module in a polynomial ring $R$, then the implementations of }, TT{topComponents}, TEX{ and }, TO{PrimaryDecomposition :: removeLowestDimension}, TEX{ are based on the following observations:}}, UL{LI{TEX{$codim Ext^d(M,R) \ge d$ for all $d$}}, LI{TEX{If $P$ is an associated prime of $M$ of codimension $d := codim P > codim M$, then $codim Ext^d(M,R) = d$ and the annihilator of $Ext^d(M,R)$ is contained in $P$}}, LI{TEX{If $codim Ext^d(M,R) = d$, then there really is an associated prime of codimension $d$.}}, LI{TEX{If $M$ is $R/I$, then $topComponents(I) = ann Ext^c(R/I,R)$, where $c = codim I$}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{PrimaryDecomposition :: removeLowestDimension}}, LI{TOH{Saturation :: saturate}}, LI{TOH{Saturation :: Ideal : Ideal}}, LI{TOH{MinimalPrimes :: radical}}}}, DIV{DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{Ways to use , TT{topComponents}, :}, UL{LI{KBD{topComponents(Ideal)}}, LI{KBD{topComponents(Module)}}, LI{KBD{topComponents(Module,ZZ)}}}}, DIV{class => waystouse, HEADER2{For the programmer}, PARA{The object , TO{PrimaryDecomposition :: topComponents},  is , SPAN{a , TO2{Macaulay2Doc :: MethodFunction, method function}}, .}}, HR{}, DIV{class => waystouse, PARA{The source of this document is in , TT{PrimaryDecomposition/doc.m2:750:0}, .}}}}

