DIV{HEADER1{Topcom,  -- interface to selected functions from topcom package}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, DIV{PARA{HREF{https://www.wm.uni-bayreuth.de/de/team/rambau_joerg/TOPCOM/index.html, Topcom}, TEX{ is mathematical software written by Jorg Rambau for computing and manipulating triangulations of polytopes and chirotopes.}}, PARA{TEX{This Macaulay2 package provides an interface for some of the functionality of this software.}}, PARA{TEX{The package is meant as an internal package, to be called by packages such as }, TO{Polyhedra :: Polyhedra}, TEX{.  It is highly recommended to use those packages, rather than calling this package directly.}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Example use of Topcom}}, DIV{UL{LI{TOH{Topcom :: An example use of TopCom}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Generating triangulations}}, DIV{UL{LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomNumTriangulations(Matrix)}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Useful functions involving specific triangulations}}, DIV{UL{LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomRegularFineTriangulation(Matrix)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix,List)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomIsRegularTriangulation(Matrix,List)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomRegularTriangulationWeights(Matrix,List)}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Useful functions involving bistellar flips}}, DIV{UL{LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomFlips(Matrix,List)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: topcomNumFlips(Matrix,List)}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Chirotope functions}}, DIV{PARA{TEX{The , ITALIC{chirotope},  of a point set (or vector set), consisting of the columns of the $d \times n$ matrix $A$, is the function which assigns to each $d+1 \times d+1$ minor of $\overline{A}$ the sign of its determinant.  Topcom encodes this into a string.  See }, TO{Topcom :: chirotopeString}, TEX{ for details about the output of this function.}}}, DIV{UL{LI{TOH{Topcom :: chirotopeString(Matrix)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: naiveChirotopeString(Matrix)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: orientedCircuits(String)}}, LI{TOH{Topcom :: orientedCocircuits(String)}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{See also}, UL{LI{TOH{Polyhedra :: Polyhedra}}, LI{TOH{Triangulations :: Triangulations}}, LI{TOH{ReflexivePolytopesDB :: ReflexivePolytopesDB}}}}, DIV{DIV{DIV{HEADER2{Author}, UL{LI{HREF{http://www.math.cornell.edu/~mike, Mike Stillman}, SPAN{ <, HREF{mailto:mike@math.cornell.edu, mike@math.cornell.edu}, >}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Version}, PARA{This documentation describes version , BOLD{0.95},  of , Topcom, , released , BOLD{13 Nov 2022}, .}}, DIV{HEADER2{Citation}, PARA{If you have used , this package,  in your research, please cite it as follows:}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{class => language-bib, @misc{TopcomSource,
  title = {{Topcom: A \emph{Macaulay2} package. Version~0.95}},
  author = {Mike Stillman},
  howpublished = {A \emph{Macaulay2} package available at
    \url{https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/tree/stable/M2/Macaulay2/packages}}
}
