DIV{HEADER1{while,  -- while loops}, UL{LI{DL{class => element, DT{Usage: }, DD{CODE{while p list x do z, class => language-macaulay2}}}}, LI{DIV{Consequences:, UL{LI{The expression , TT{p},  is repeatedly evaluated.  As long as the result is true, , TT{x},  is evaluated and its value is saved, and , TT{z},  is evaluated and its value is discarded.  When the value of , TT{p},  is false, then the loop terminates, and the list of values of , TT{x},  is returned as the value of the entire expression.}}}}}, DIV{HEADER2{Description}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i1 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list i^2 do i = i+1

o2 = {0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81}

o2 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{The , TT{list x},  clause may be omitted, in which case no list is accumulated, and , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: null},  is returned as the value of the expression.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i3 : i = 0 ; while i < 4 do (print i; i = i+1)
0
1
2
3, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{Alternatively, the , TT{do z},  clause may be omitted.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i5 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list (i = i+1; i^2)

o6 = {1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81, 100}

o6 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{Observe the use of the semicolon (see , TT{;}, ) in the expression above.}, PARA{If , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: continue},  is executed by , TT{x},  then execution of , TT{x},  is interrupted, no value is added to the list, and iteration of the loop continues.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i7 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list (i = i+1; if odd i then continue; i^2)

o8 = {4, 16, 36, 64, 100}

o8 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{If , TT{continue w},  is executed by , TT{x},  then execution of , TT{x},  is interrupted, the value of , TT{w},  is added to the list, and iteration of the loop continues.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i9 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list (i = i+1; if odd i then continue 1234; i^2)

o10 = {1234, 4, 1234, 16, 1234, 36, 1234, 64, 1234, 100}

o10 : List, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{  If , TT{break v},  is executed by , TT{x}, , then the loop is stopped and , TT{v},  is returned as its value.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i11 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list (i = i+1; if i == 5 then break i; i^2)

o12 = 5, class => language-macaulay2}}}}}, PARA{If , TO{Macaulay2Doc :: break},  is executed by , TT{x}, , then the loop is stopped and the list accumulated so far is returned as the value.}, TABLE{class => examples, TR{TD{PRE{CODE{i13 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 list (i = i+1; if i == 5 then break; i^2)

